2026-06-25 13:01:20,672 | AGENT | TechnicalArchitect Agent answered: To meet the City of Belval's technical requirements, I propose an architecture based on our company's existing capabilities and technology stack. We can design an artificial intelligence solution using our primary domains of expertise: AI/ML systems, Cloud architecture, API integration, Data engineering, and Cybersecurity.

Firstly, to integrate with existing systems such as business software (civil status, town planning), electronic management of documents (EDM), and user directories, we can utilize API-type interfaces. Our experience with API gateways like Kong, Apigee, and AWS API Gateway will enable us to securely manage API interactions between the AI solution and these existing systems.

For the AI solution itself, we can leverage our expertise in AI/ML systems, specifically our experience with LLM models such as Mistral 7B, LLaMA 3, CamemBERT, and Falcon. We can fine-tune these models using our knowledge of fine-tuning methods like LoRA, QLoRA, and Full fine-tune to achieve high accuracy in providing recommendations or proposals.

To ensure response times under 2 seconds for current requests, we can utilize our inference servers like vLLM, Ollama, or TGI (Hugging Face) to optimize the performance of our AI models. Our vector databases such as Qdrant, Weaviate, or pgvector can also be used to efficiently store and retrieve data.

To achieve high availability (99.9%), we can design a cloud-based architecture using our experience with cloud providers like OVHcloud, Scaleway, Outscale (SecNumCloud), and Azure (EU regions). Our containerisation expertise with Docker, Kubernetes (K8s), and Helm will enable us to orchestrate and manage the deployment of the AI solution. Additionally, we can use monitoring tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack to ensure the solution's performance and availability.

For data sovereignty and security, we can ensure that all data is hosted exclusively on SecNumCloud infrastructure or equivalent, as required by the City of Belval. Our experience with encryption methods like AES-256 at rest and TLS 1.3 in transit will guarantee the protection of sensitive data. We can also implement network security patterns like Zero-trust, VLAN segmentation, and mTLS between services to prevent unauthorized access.

To ensure explicability and transparency in the AI solution's recommendations or proposals, we can utilize our explainability tools such as SHAP, LIME, chain-of-thought prompting, and RAG source citation. These tools will enable us to provide insights into the decision-making process of the AI models, thereby ensuring trust and accountability.

